// A recipe, written from md-docs/recipes/serve-with-apache.md by scripts/docsite/recipes.py;
// edit the recipe, not this file.
page RecipeServeWithApache(path: "/recipes/serve-with-apache", title: "Serve a site with Apache — Recipes", description: "Serve a WebFluent build with Apache: an .htaccess file with the 404 page, a single-page fallback, security headers and compressed files.") {
    RecipeShell("Serve a site with Apache", summary: "This recipe serves a WebFluent build with Apache, configured by an `.htaccess` file that ships with the build.  You need an Apache host with `mod_rewrite` and `mod_headers`, and a `build/` folder from `wf build` ([Install wf on a build machine](/recipes/install-wf-in-ci)).  Put this in `public/.htaccess`:", outputs: ["website", "app"], since: "", recipes: RECIPE_INDEX, sections: [Anchor(id: "how-it-works", label: "How it works"), Anchor(id: "check-it", label: "Check it"), Anchor(id: "variations", label: "Variations")], related: [RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Install wf on a build machine", to: "/recipes/install-wf-in-ci"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Use environment values, and keep secrets out", to: "/recipes/environments-and-secrets"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Deploy to GitHub Pages", to: "/recipes/deploy-to-github-pages")], source: "md-docs/recipes/serve-with-apache.md", how: true, hasVariations: true) {
        code {
            CodeBlock("Options -MultiViews\nRewriteEngine On\n# A single-page build:\n# RewriteCond %\{REQUEST_FILENAME\} !-f\n# RewriteRule ^ /index.html [L]\nErrorDocument 404 /404.html\nHeader always set X-Content-Type-Options \"nosniff\"\nHeader always set X-Frame-Options \"DENY\"\nHeader always set Referrer-Policy \"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\"", title: "apache")
        }
        variations {
            Markdown("Compress the text files one of two ways:\n\n- Turn on `mod_deflate`, which compresses on the way out. This is the simplest, and covers every text file.\n- Serve the `.gz` files the build wrote, so Apache compresses nothing itself. `Options MultiViews` does not do it: content negotiation only runs when the file asked for does not exist, and `app.js` does. Add these lines after `RewriteEngine On`, before the single-page lines, as Apache's own `mod_deflate` documentation does it:\n\n  ```apache # The build's app.js.gz for app.js, when the browser accepts gzip RewriteCond \"%\{HTTP:Accept-Encoding\}\" \"gzip\" RewriteCond \"%\{REQUEST_FILENAME\}.gz\" -s RewriteRule \"^(.*)\\.(css|js)$\" \"$1.$2.gz\" [QSA]\n\n  # Sent with the right type, and not compressed a second time RewriteRule \"\\.css\\.gz$\" \"-\" [T=text/css,E=no-gzip:1] RewriteRule \"\\.js\\.gz$\" \"-\" [T=text/javascript,E=no-gzip:1]\n\n  <FilesMatch \"\\.(css|js)\\.gz$\"> Header append Content-Encoding gzip Header append Vary Accept-Encoding </FilesMatch> ```\n\n  This covers the scripts and stylesheets, the largest files. Pages are asked for by their folder (`/contact/`), which the rule cannot see as a file, so leave `mod_deflate` on for HTML.")

        }
        Markdown("Then upload `build/` to the site's document root.\n\n1. The build copies `public/.htaccess` to the root of `build/`, so it lands in the document root with the site.\n2. For a single-page build, uncomment the two rewrite lines: a path that is no file is answered with `index.html`, where the router draws the page.\n3. `ErrorDocument 404 /404.html` serves the page whose `path` is `*`.\n4. The `Header` lines send security headers the build writes to `build/_headers` ([Set cache and security headers](/recipes/cache-and-security-headers#set-security-headers)).")

        Heading("Check it", id: "check-it").h2

        Markdown("`curl -I` a page and check for `X-Content-Type-Options`, `X-Frame-Options` and `Referrer-Policy`. With the `.gz` rules, `curl -sI -H \"Accept-Encoding: gzip\" https://example.com/app.js` answers `Content-Encoding: gzip` and `Content-Type: text/javascript`. Open a path that does not exist and check that you get the site's `404.html`. Then go through [Check a deploy](/recipes/check-a-deploy).")

    }
}
